{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c49b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06ff2-73b2-7750-92a2-8ff950295c9d"},"sequence":168,"recorded_at":1780531400000331,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"1b11d441-f4bd-4331-a485-e0ecf0af0397","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"1b11d441-f4bd-4331-a485-e0ecf0af0397","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"1b11d441-f4bd-4331-a485-e0ecf0af0397"},"call_id":"call_01a06ff2fe737d41846cc87325db8634","text":"Read text file `internal/terminalbackend/refusal_arm_inventory_test.go`.\n(99 line(s) above)\n100|// deriveRefusalArms walks every production file of this package (every\n101|// *.go except *_test.go, so a new production file is scanned without\n102|// anyone remembering it) and returns every refusal arm in source order.\n103|// It fails closed: an unparseable file, a non-static code or detail, and\n104|// an empty result are all fatal, never an empty table.\n105|//\n106|// Coverage is declaration-complete, not FuncDecl-complete: every FuncDecl\n107|// body (including nested func literals, methods, and init) plus every\n108|// package-level var initializer is scanned, so a refusal arm hiding in a\n109|// package-level `var f = func() *Error {...}` is derived like any other.\n110|// Constructor references outside direct-call position (`refuse :=\n111|// mismatchf`) are rejected outright by rejectConstructorAliases below:\n112|// an aliased refusal cannot be inventoried, so it fails the suite rather\n113|// than shipping silently.\n114|func deriveRefusalArms(t *testing.T) []refusalArm {\n115|\tt.Helper()\n116|\n117|\tmatches, err := filepath.Glob(\"*.go\")\n118|\tif err != nil {\n119|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"glob production files: %v\", err)\n120|\t}\n121|\tvar production []string\n122|\tfor _, match := range matches {\n123|\t\tif !strings.HasSuffix(match, \"_test.go\") {\n124|\t\t\tproduction = append(production, match)\n125|\t\t}\n126|\t}\n127|\tif len(production) == 0 {\n128|\t\tt.Fatal(\"derived zero production files; the scanner is broken, not the package\")\n129|\t}\n130|\n131|\tvar arms []refusalArm\n132|\tparsed := 0\n133|\tfor _, name := range production {\n134|\t\tfileSet := token.NewFileSet()\n135|\t\tfile, err := parser.ParseFile(fileSet, name, nil, 0)\n136|\t\tif err != nil {\n137|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"parse %s: %v; an unparseable derivation proves nothing\", name, err)\n138|\t\t}\n139|\t\tparsed++\n140|\t\tcollect := func(functionName string, root ast.Node) {\n141|\t\t\tast.Inspect(root, func(node ast.Node) bool {\n142|\t\t\t\tswitch expression := node.(type) {\n143|\t\t\t\tcase *ast.UnaryExpr:\n144|\t\t\t\t\tif expression.Op != token.AND {\n145|\t\t\t\t\t\treturn true\n146|\t\t\t\t\t}\n147|\t\t\t\t\tliteral, ok := expression.X.(*ast.CompositeLit)\n148|\t\t\t\t\tif !ok {\n149|\t\t\t\t\t\treturn true\n150|\t\t\t\t\t}\n151|\t\t\t\t\tidentifier, ok := literal.Type.(*ast.Ident)\n152|\t\t\t\t\tif !ok || identifier.Name != \"Error\" {\n153|\t\t\t\t\t\treturn true\n154|\t\t\t\t\t}\n155|\t\t\t\t\tcode, detail := \"\", \"\"\n156|\t\t\t\t\tfor _, element := range literal.Elts {\n157|\t\t\t\t\t\tpair, ok := element.(*ast.KeyValueExpr)\n158|\t\t\t\t\t\tif !ok {\n159|\t\t\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n160|\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n161|\t\t\t\t\t\tkey, ok := pair.Key.(*ast.Ident)\n162|\t\t\t\t\t\tif !ok {\n163|\t\t\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n164|\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n165|\t\t\t\t\t\tswitch key.Name {\n166|\t\t\t\t\t\tcase \"Code\":\n167|\t\t\t\t\t\t\tsymbol, ok := pair.Value.(*ast.Ident)\n168|\t\t\t\t\t\t\tif !ok {\n169|\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"%s: refusal code is not a static Code symbol; \"+\n170|\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"a computed code cannot be inventoried\", functionName)\n171|\t\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n172|\t\t\t\t\t\t\tcode = symbol.Name\n173|\t\t\t\t\t\tcase \"Detail\":\n174|\t\t\t\t\t\t\tdetail = staticDetail(t, functionName, pair.Value)\n175|\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n176|\t\t\t\t\t}\n177|\t\t\t\t\tif code == \"\" || detail == \"\" {\n178|\t\t\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"%s: refusal without a static code and detail; \"+\n179|\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"the inventory cannot name what it cannot read\", functionName)\n180|\t\t\t\t\t}\n181|\t\t\t\t\tarms = append(arms, refusalArm{\n182|\t\t\t\t\t\tfile: name, function: functionName, code: code, detail: detail,\n183|\t\t\t\t\t})\n184|\t\t\t\tcase *ast.CallExpr:\n185|\t\t\t\t\tidentifier, ok := expression.Fun.(*ast.Ident)\n186|\t\t\t\t\tif !ok || !constructorFunctions[identifier.Name] {\n187|\t\t\t\t\t\treturn true\n188|\t\t\t\t\t}\n189|\t\t\t\t\tif len(expression.Args) != 1 {\n190|\t\t\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"%s: %s with %d arguments; Detail must be a single \"+\n191|\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"static literal and never interpolate local data, and a \"+\n192|\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"variadic detail cannot be inventoried\",\n193|\t\t\t\t\t\t\tfunctionName, identifier.Name, len(expression.Args))\n194|\t\t\t\t\t}\n195|\t\t\t\t\tliteral, ok := expression.Args[0].(*ast.BasicLit)\n196|\t\t\t\t\tif !ok || literal.Kind != token.STRING {\n197|\t\t\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"%s: %s detail is not a static string literal; \"+\n198|\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"a computed detail cannot be inventoried\", functionName, identifier.Name)\n199|\t\t\t\t\t}\n200|\t\t\t\t\tdetail, err := strconv.Unquote(literal.Value)\n201|\t\t\t\t\tif err != nil {\n202|\t\t\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"%s: unquote detail: %v\", functionName, err)\n203|\t\t\t\t\t}\n204|\t\t\t\t\tcode := \"CodeMismatch\"\n205|\t\t\t\t\tif identifier.Name == \"integrityFailure\" {\n206|\t\t\t\t\t\tcode = \"CodeIntegrityFailure\"\n207|\t\t\t\t\t}\n208|\t\t\t\t\tarms = append(arms, refusalArm{\n209|\t\t\t\t\t\tfile: name, function: functionName, code: code, detail: detail,\n210|\t\t\t\t\t})\n211|\t\t\t\t}\n212|\t\t\t\treturn true\n213|\t\t\t})\n214|\t\t}\n215|\t\tfor _, declaration := range file.Decls {\n216|\t\t\tswitch decl := declaration.(type) {\n217|\t\t\tcase *ast.FuncDecl:\n218|\t\t\t\tif decl.Body == nil {\n219|\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n220|\t\t\t\t}\n221|\t\t\t\tif constructorFunctions[decl.Name.Name] {\n222|\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n223|\t\t\t\t}\n224|\t\t\t\tfunctionName := decl.Name.Name\n225|\t\t\t\tif decl.Recv != nil && len(decl.Recv.List) > 0 {\n226|\t\t\t\t\tfunctionName = receiverTypeName(decl.Recv.List[0].Type) + \".\" + functionName\n227|\t\t\t\t}\n228|\t\t\t\tcollect(functionName, decl.Body)\n229|\t\t\tcase *ast.GenDecl:\n230|\t\t\t\t// Package-level initializers execute outside any FuncDecl,\n231|\t\t\t\t// so a func literal (or a bare &Error{}) assigned to a\n232|\t\t\t\t// package var would otherwise ship invisible. Attribute\n233|\t\t\t\t// its arms to the declared variable name.\n234|\t\t\t\tfor _, spec := range decl.Specs {\n235|\t\t\t\t\tvalue, ok := spec.(*ast.ValueSpec)\n236|\t\t\t\t\tif !ok {\n237|\t\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n238|\t\t\t\t\t}\n239|\t\t\t\t\tfunctionName := \"var\"\n240|\t\t\t\t\tif len(value.Names) > 0 {\n241|\t\t\t\t\t\tfunctionName = value.Names[0].Name\n242|\t\t\t\t\t}\n243|\t\t\t\t\tfor _, item := range value.Values {\n244|\t\t\t\t\t\tcollect(functionName, item)\n245|\t\t\t\t\t}\n246|\t\t\t\t}\n247|\t\t\t}\n248|\t\t}\n249|\t\trejectConstructorAliases(t, file, name)\n250|\t}\n251|\t_ = parsed\n252|\tif len(arms) == 0 {\n253|\t\tt.Fatal(\"derived zero refusal arms from the package sources; the scanner is broken, not the package\")\n254|\t}\n255|\toccurrences := make(map[refusalArm]int)\n256|\tfor index := range arms {\n257|\t\tkey := arms[index]\n258|\t\tkey.occurrence = 0\n259|\t\toccurrences[key]++\n260|\t\tarms[index].occurrence = occurrences[key]\n261|\t}\n262|\treturn arms\n263|}\n264|\n265|// rejectConstructorAliases fails the suite when a refusal constructor\n266|// (mismatchf, integrityFailure) is referenced outside direct-call\n267|// position. `refuse := mismatchf; refuse(\"…\")` ships a reachable arm the\n268|// arm derivation above cannot attribute to a static call site, so the\n269|// reference itself is the violation: call the constructor directly.\n270|// The constructors' own declarations are excluded; their bodies are the\n271|// funnel, not arms. Any other use — alias, argument, field, shadow —\n272|// fails closed, because no legitimate production shape needs it.\n273|func rejectConstructorAliases(t *testing.T, file *ast.File, name string) {\n274|\tt.Helper()\n275|\n276|\tallowed := map[token.Pos]bool{}\n277|\tast.Inspect(file, func(node ast.Node) bool {\n278|\t\tdeclaration, ok := node.(*ast.FuncDecl)\n279|\t\tif !ok {\n280|\t\t\tif call, ok := node.(*ast.CallExpr); ok {\n281|\t\t\t\tif identifier, ok := call.Fun.(*ast.Ident); ok && constructorFunctions[identifier.Name] {\n282|\t\t\t\t\tallowed[identifier.Pos()] = true\n283|\t\t\t\t}\n284|\t\t\t}\n285|\t\t\treturn true\n286|\t\t}\n287|\t\tif constructorFunctions[declaration.Name.Name] {\n288|\t\t\tallowed[declaration.Name.Pos()] = true\n289|\t\t\treturn false\n290|\t\t}\n291|\t\treturn true\n292|\t})\n293|\tast.Inspect(file, func(node ast.Node) bool {\n294|\t\tdeclaration, ok := node.(*ast.FuncDecl)\n295|\t\tif ok && constructorFunctions[declaration.Name.Name] {\n296|\t\t\treturn false\n297|\t\t}\n298|\t\tidentifier, ok := node.(*ast.Ident)\n299|\t\tif !ok || !constructorFunctions[identifier.Name] || allowed[identifier.Pos()] {\n300|\t\t\treturn true\n301|\t\t}\n302|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"%s: constructor %q referenced outside direct-call position; \"+\n303|\t\t\t\"an aliased refusal cannot be inventoried, call it directly\", name, identifier.Name)\n304|\t\treturn true\n305|\t})\n306|}\n307|\n308|// receiverTypeName renders a method receiver type to its bare name.\n309|func receiverTypeName(expression ast.Expr) string {\n310|\tswitch typed := expression.(type) {\n311|\tcase *ast.Ident:\n312|\t\treturn typed.Name\n313|\tcase *ast.StarExpr:\n314|\t\treturn receiverTypeName(typed.X)\n315|\tdefault:\n316|\t\treturn \"unknown\"\n317|\t}\n318|}\n319|\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c49d","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06ff2-73b2-7750-92a2-8ff950295c9d"},"sequence":169,"recorded_at":1780531400000333,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"1b11d441-f4bd-4331-a485-e0ecf0af0397","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"1b11d441-f4bd-4331-a485-e0ecf0af0397","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"1b11d441-f4bd-4331-a485-e0ecf0af0397"},"call_id":"call_01a06ff2ff2b7541ba5118ebb8460a0d","text":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-4-1\",\n  \"command\": \"grep -n \\\"closed-set\\\\|closed set\\\\|P11\\\\|C20\\\\|legacyForward\\\\|HistoricalTranslation\\\\|conformanceOperations\\\" LOGBOOK.md | head -20\",\n  \"description\": \"Find logbook false claim\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"469:- DISCLOSURE, not repaired here: `WorkspaceSnapshot.members` and `GitIndex.entries` enforce uniqueness the pinned document declares nowhere — an equal `workspace_id` and an equal `(path, stage)` pair respectively. Both sit in `closed_shapes.go`, in sections owned by `TASK-260830-uqnwmi`, inside a reviewed and accepted candidate. They are recorded as disclosed strengthenings with their exact undeclared refusal and routed, and the disclosed set is asserted exactly against the artifact in both directions so a fourth cannot appear silently.\\n738:- BOUNDS (carried forward, not dropped): the inventory kills every arm-deleting mutant by construction, so post-leaf-3 mutation scores are NOT comparable to leaf 2's 91/95 — stated in the inventory file's Stated bounds block and here. Attribution drift survives via the entry+code fallback — live example `CheckTransition`'s dead `\\\"operation vocabulary\\\"` arm resolving through `ParseOperation`'s test — also stated there. Declined closure: P13 (empty-ID `ProjectToLegacy` still refuses, different wire code). P11 (legacy escape name) is no longer declined: C20 (`legacyForward` gains `\\\"screen\\\"`) is killed by `TestLegacyReverseProjectionExistsOnlyForThePair`, so the closed-set property is pinned.\\n748:- FIX (G4): new `TestDerivedVocabulariesAreExactlyTheAdmittedSets` derives all four parser vocabularies (states, operations, effects, transports) from switch-case lists resolved through string consts, both directions plus size, and pins `conformanceOperations` to the derived operation set — the \\\"pinned by\\\" citation now holds. Refused samples restated as sampling bounds over the unbounded string domain and extended with the reviewer's exact survivor strings (`detached`, `detach`, `input_reopened`, `ssh_tunnel`), each now behaviorally refused.\\n749:- BOUNDS (recorded, not closed): W11 (DigestFile allowlist is function-wide, no detail pin), W13 (bespoke error types outside both spellings), mismatchf format-verb interpolation (derivation now fatals on any constructor call without exactly one string-literal argument — zero such sites today; vet catches non-constant formats). P11 stale bound dropped (C20 killed); P13 declined closure stands.\\n752:- SCOPE: `internal/terminalbackend/conformance_test.go` (G1/G3-comment/G4), `internal_pin_test.go` (G3 pin), `refusal_arm_inventory_test.go` (G2 twin + single-arg assertion + bounds), `LOGBOOK.md` (this entry + P11 correction). No production change, no arm-table change, 193/193 undisturbed.\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 2510,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 628,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"bash","outcome":"success"}}}
