n732|### TASK-260830-1snnef round-1 rework: four sampled closures, closed by derivation\n733|- FINDING (F1): The refusal-arm derivation walked FuncDecl bodies only, so a package-level `var f = func() *Error {…}` arm and an aliased constructor (`refuse := mismatchf`) each shipped reachable with a new detail while both inventory tests stayed green. Both shapes measured empty in the tree, so the 193/193 ratio held while the closure claim did not.\n734|- FIX (F1, preferred over a caveat): the derivation now scans every FuncDecl body plus every package-level var initializer (attributed to the variable name), and `rejectConstructorAliases` fatals on any constructor reference outside direct-call position. Replayed both reviewer probes copy-aside with shasum-verified restore: A1 fails the bijection (194 derived vs 193 rows), A2 fatals at the alias. Zero table change — both shapes are still empty in the tree.\n735|- FIX (F2): `TestCheckErrorAllowedRefusesEveryUnlistedCode` was a 3–5-code sample named as a complement. It now derives the complement: a full-row mirror table (`allowedErrorCodesByOperation`, all ten rows exact) is proved a subset of production by the exhaustive admit test and production is proved a subset of the mirror over the pinned catalog (`catalog.Current().Errors`) by the refusal loop, with a mirror-inside-catalog pin and fail-closed empty-domain guards. P20 (admit `terminal_backend_unavailable` for all ten ops) now fails the suite. Non-catalog strings are an unbounded domain: three probes pin the shape with the sampling bound stated, not claimed as closure.\n736|- FIX (F3): added `CheckAttachResult(false, false, auth{InputAuthorized:true})` — the case only the third conjunct catches. Dropping `resultInputAuthorized != auth.InputAuthorized` now fails the suite.\n737|- FIX (F4): attach expiry pinned from both sides — admitted one second before `expires`, refused exactly at it. `!now.Before(expires)` → `now.After(expires)` now fails the suite.\n738|- BOUNDS (carried forward, not dropped): the inventory kills every arm-deleting mutant by construction, so post-leaf-3 mutation scores are NOT comparable to leaf 2's 91/95 — stated in the inventory file's Stated bounds block and here. Attribution drift survives via the entry+code fallback — live example `CheckTransition`'s dead `\"operation vocabulary\"` arm resolving through `ParseOperation`'s test — also stated there. Declined closure: P13 (empty-ID `ProjectToLegacy` still refuses, different wire code). P11 (legacy escape name) is no longer declined: C20 (`legacyForward` gains `\"screen\"`) is killed by `TestLegacyReverseProjectionExistsOnlyForThePair`, so the closed-set property is pinned.\n739|- EVIDENCE: A1/A2/P8/P16/P20 replayed, each red with exit 1, tree restored byte-identical (shasum). Full gates re-run below.\n740|- SCOPE: `internal/terminalbackend/refusal_arm_inventory_test.go` (derivation + bounds), `conformance_test.go` (F2–F4); `LOGBOOK.md` (this entry, 89.9% correction). No production change, no table change, README sentence stands as written now that the derivation covers it.\n741|- STATUS: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (14/14), `-race` on terminalbackend exit 0, `go vet ./...` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` exit 0 (`acceptance_cases=76`, section coverage unchanged). Package coverage 90.0% statements measured on this rework tree (test-only additions vs the rev-1 tree the reviewer measured at 89.9%). Rework left uncommitted in the working tree per the brief (board checkpoints, no commit).\n742|\n743|### TASK-260830-1snnef round-2 rework: three sampled closures of one family, closed by derivation\n744|- FINDING (G2): `TestPlainErrorsLiveOnlyInTheirTwoFunctions` walked FuncDecl bodies only — the exact walk `deriveRefusalArms` was extended past in round 1, 200 lines above in the same file. Identical `errors.New` text was red in a FuncDecl and green in a package-level var (W5b), `fmt.Errorf` likewise (W9b), var func literal likewise (W16).\n745|- FIX (G2): the sibling walk gained the same GenDecl/ValueSpec loop (shared `isPlainErrorConstruction` helper, receiver-qualified method names). Twin-hunt over the story boundary (`internal/terminalbackend` AST walks): `deriveRefusalArms` already extended, `rejectConstructorAliases` inspects whole files, `productionCodeSymbols` walks package-level const GenDecls by construction, `testBodies`/`predicateCodes` are func-scoped by convention and fail closed, the platform funnel is function-scoped by design. No other twin. Bonus kill: an unused package-level plain-error var (W18 shape) is now red too — its initializer runs at package init, so the construction is real.\n746|- FIX (G1): `TestCheckStatusResultEnforcesLookupRules` now derives the complement — every state the production parser admits (`derivedParserVocabulary` over the switch-case list) outside parked/active is refused with attach evidenced; parked/active admitted. C13/C26/C27/C28/C29 each red, C30 still red.\n747|- FIX (G3): new internal `TestReplicationMembersAreExactlyTheClosedTable` pins the live `replicationMembers` map in both directions plus the size (64 members). C40c (add) and C40-init-injection red there; C40b/C40d red there and at the entry. External test comment restated to its half (want subset production) with the reverse cited.\n748|- FIX (G4): new `TestDerivedVocabulariesAreExactlyTheAdmittedSets` derives all four parser vocabularies (states, operations, effects, transports) from switch-case lists resolved through string consts, both directions plus size, and pins `conformanceOperations` to the derived operation set — the \"pinned by\" citation now holds. Refused samples restated as sampling bounds over the unbounded string domain and extended with the reviewer's exact survivor strings (`detached`, `detach`, `input_reopened`, `ssh_tunnel`), each now behaviorally refused.\n749|- BOUNDS (recorded, not closed): W11 (DigestFile allowlist is function-wide, no detail pin), W13 (bespoke error types outside both sp