{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4d3","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06ff2-73b2-7750-92a2-8ff950295c9d"},"sequence":196,"recorded_at":1780531400000387,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"1b11d441-f4bd-4331-a485-e0ecf0af0397","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"1b11d441-f4bd-4331-a485-e0ecf0af0397","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"1b11d441-f4bd-4331-a485-e0ecf0af0397"},"call_id":"call_01a06ff30c907bb1b133a39d4a9b8513","text":"Read text file `LOGBOOK.md`.\n(699 line(s) above)\n700|- FINDING: A completeness gate over a *pattern* must also police the pattern. Deriving the expected set is not enough if the extraction rule silently excludes a whole syntactic class.\n701|- FIX: Second funnel `projectionOwnershipRefusal` (`internal/localstore/projection.go:117`) keeps the refusal decision at its call site while preserving the owner-only cause; every projection refusal rerouted through a funnel. Gate now derives two properties — funnel sites need an exercised negative path beneath `openProjection`, AND no projection-owned source may raise a refusal outside a funnel. Build-context filtering added so a platform-specific refusal is not demanded from a platform that cannot run it.\n702|- ANOMALY: I reproduced the identical bug class inside the fix. The new unrouted check sat behind `typed.Fun.(*ast.Ident)`, and `fmt.Errorf` is a `*ast.SelectorExpr`, so the exact class stayed invisible in code written specifically to catch it. First run of mutant m41 exited 0. Reading the new gate would not have found this; only the behaviour-preserving mutant did.\n703|- DECISION: Assume \"unreachable\" last, not first. One clause presumed unreachable — the non-regular branch of `ensureProjectionFileModes` — is drivable through the real production entry by replacing a sidecar with a FIFO in the post-rebuild hook. Only three clauses are genuine TOCTOU re-checks, each annotated with the earlier check that owns the reachable case.\n704|- SCOPE: `internal/localstore/projection.go`, `projection_lock_unix.go`, `projection_refusal_inventory_test.go`, new `projection_unix_test.go`, `README.md`.\n705|- STATUS: Resolved. 15 mutants, 13 red as required, 1 designed control green, 1 documented subsumed green. TASK-260830-3amrl9 rev5, handed to review.\n706|\n707|### 2113 — A gate must prove its own coverage; so must a mutation sweep\n708|- ROOT CAUSE: `requireMemberSet` was a byte-identical duplicate of `requireExactMembers`. `TestConstraintEnumerationMatchesRequireExactMembers` scanned only the latter by name, so `WorkspaceMember.*`, every Session Event payload, `Observation Event`, and `ObservationCounts` carried zero per-member enumeration rows while the README claimed a complete inventory.\n709|- FINDING: That blind spot is why a real defect reached review — `internal/canonicaljson/core_records.go` `validateTerminalV4Payload` validated `terminal_backend_id` with `requireString` only, so `CalculateObjectIdentity` attested `AX.TMUX`, `../../etc/passwd`, an embedded NUL and 5000 chars. SPEC.md:890 (§4.B) pins it to 1–128 ASCII bytes matching `[a-z][a-z0-9]*(?:[.-][a-z0-9]+)*`.\n710|- FIX: Duplicate deleted, all 5 call sites collapsed onto `requireExactMembers`. Grammar enforced by `requireTerminalBackendID`. `TestRequireExactMembersIsTheOnlyClosedMemberGate` now derives every function emitting a closed-member refusal and fails unless that set is exactly `{requireExactMembers}`; the scanned file set is derived from the package directory, not a hand-written list.\n711|- ANOMALY: The mutation harness aborted mid-run on the zsh reserved variable `status`, after applying mutant 1 but before its restore. The next run took its baseline backup from that mutated tree, so all 12 mutants were behavioural no-ops against an already-red mask and every one reported KILLED for the wrong reason. Caught only because the full-repo run afterwards failed.\n712|- FIX: Harness refuses to sweep unless the baseline is green, and reports `NOT-APPLIED` for any mutant that left the tree unchanged. Re-run: 12/12 killed, 0 survivors.\n713|- DECISION: Session Event payload members are pinned by mechanical extraction from the pinned SPEC's four `Exact payload members` tables into `internal/canonicaljson/testdata/session-event-payload-members.md` (39 event types, 204 declarations) rather than hand-listed across 134 version×event shapes.\n714|- FINDING: The first extractor split on `</code>,` and silently dropped members followed by a bare `(G2)` annotation, losing `clone.planned.projection_plan_id` and `clone.failed.materialization_id`. The new derivation test caught it; review had not. Parse one `<code>` span per declaration.\n715|- NOTE: General property, applies to every derived gate — an inventory must assert that the set of constructs it scans is complete for the package, and a mutation sweep must assert its baseline is green. A gate that cannot fail when someone adds a second copy of a check is decoration, and a mutant that \"kills\" an already-red mask proves nothing.\n716|- SCOPE: `internal/canonicaljson/`, `internal/traceability/ownership.v0.5.0.json`, `README.md`\n717|- STATUS: Resolved; TASK-260830-1tax26 handed to review as revision 2.\n718|\n719|### TASK-260830-1zvmw7 round-3: three unpinned arms, found by enumeration not by review\n720|- FINDING: The round-2 verdict named three survivors (S6/S7/S8), but the rework does not rely on the reviewer's list: I extracted every `mismatchf(\"...\")`/`Detail: \"...\"` string from `internal/terminalbackend/manifest.go` and counted assertions of each detail across the three terminalbackend test files. Exactly five details had zero hits: the three fixed here plus `document identity` (x2, reviewer-declared practically unreachable) and `registry unavailable` (M92 near-equivalent) — both already in the stated bounds. No other file-unique arm is unpinned.\n721|- FIX: Three table rows in `internal/terminalbackend/manifest_test.go`, no production change: `TestReconcileRefusals/static claim without manifest` (probe claims graceful_stop static while the manifest omits it; value/evidence intact so only that arm rejects), `TestEvidenceDocumentRefusals/bad platform` (`plan9`), `TestManifestDocumentRefusals/non-object claim` (string element).\n722|- EVIDENCE: Each mutant grep-anchored (count==1), vet-checked, reverted byte-identical. H1 and H2 fail with `error = <nil>` (admission, no slide); H3 fails arm-blind at `document members`, as predicted — still fail-closed, now arm-pinned. Full `go test ./...` green, package coverage 88.6% -> 88.9%.\n723|\n724|### TASK-260830-1snnef: terminal conformance harness and derived refusal-arm inventory\n725|- FINDING: Deriving the refusal arms before writing the inventory found two genuinely unwitnessed arms, not review hypotheticals: `Registry.AdmitProbe` on a nil registry (nil check first, so no fixture needed) and `ParseEvidence` on malformed `observed_at`/`expires_at` (timestamp parse precedes identity recomputation, proven by the new cases passing). Both now have tests. Seven further arms are dead by construction with the bound stated, not inferred: two `evidence canonical bytes` arms (serializes a fixed string/bool/null map; `encoding/json` and JCS cannot fail on it) and five re-parse `document timestamp` arms after an already-validated member (this leaf's three plus `checkEvidenceLiveness`'s two, pinned as exactly these five).\n726|- FINDING: The single dynamic-detail funnel is `Registration.validate` wrapping `validatePlatforms` via `err.Error()`. The inventory pins the funneled set exactly (three details, derived from the AST both ways) and allowlists plain-error construction to `validatePlatforms` and `DigestFile` only, with `DigestFile` failures asserted never-`*Error` behaviorally. A second funnel or a new plain-error refusal site is a red.\n727|- DECISION: Row resolution is detail-mention OR (entry-mention AND wire-or-verified-predicate-mention), with predicates verified from the production AST. External tests assert codes through predicates with isolating fixtures; demanding detail strings there would misdescribe the battery. Misattribution (right detail, wrong test) remains a review finding — three such rows were caught by reading the generated table, not by the gate.\n728|- EVIDENCE: 8 copy-aside mutants, each grep-confirmed present and restored `cmp`-clean: M1 replays the reviewer's exact attack (new arm, new detail) and fails forward naming the arm plus reverse on the count; M2 reuses an existing detail in a new function and fails on the function key; M3/M4/M7 narrow rather than delete and fail at `error = <nil>`; M5 (deleted relay refusal) fails the gate and both inventory directions via the stale row; M6 (swapped legacy map) fails three translation tests; M9 (deleted table row) fails forward plus the bijection. 8/8 killed, 0 survivors.\n729|- SCOPE: `internal/terminalbackend/conformance.go`, `conformance_test.go`, `refusal_arm_inventory_test.go` (new); `manifest_test.go` (+2 evidence-timestamp cases), `terminalbackend_test.go` (+5 wire codes); `internal/traceability/ownership.v0.5.0.json` (+`terminal-lifecycle-conformance` acceptance case, 75->76), `traceability.go` (projection digest), `traceability_test.go`, `cmd/tracecheck/main_test.go`, `README.md`. Section bindings untouched: still `unevidenced` with honest gaps, no clause-level claims added.\n730|- STATUS: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (14 packages), `-race` exit 0 (14 packages), `go vet ./...` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` exit 0. Package coverage 89.9% statements (reviewer-measured on the rev-1 tree; 90.0% was my rounding error). New files left untracked in the working tree; no commit (board checkpoints). TASK-260830-1snnef handed to review.\n731|\n732|### TASK-260830-1snnef round-1 rework: four sampled closures, closed by derivation\n733|- FINDING (F1): The refusal-arm derivation walked FuncDecl bodies only, so a package-level `var f = func() *Error {…}` arm and an aliased constructor (`refuse := mismatchf`) each shipped reachable with a new detail while both inventory tests stayed green. Both shapes measured empty in the tree, so the 193/193 ratio held while the closure claim did not.\n734|- FIX (F1, preferred over a caveat): the derivation now scans every FuncDecl body plus every package-level var initializer (attributed to the variable name), and `rejectConstructorAliases` fatals on any constructor reference outside direct-call position. Replayed both reviewer probes copy-aside with shasum-verified restore: A1 fails the bijection (194 derived vs 193 rows), A2 fatals at the alias. Zero table change — both shapes are still empty in the tree.\n735|- FIX (F2): `TestCheckErrorAllowedRefusesEveryUnlistedCode` was a 3–5-code sample named as a complement. It now derives the complement: a full-row mirror table (`allowedErrorCodesByOperation`, all ten rows exact) is proved a subset of production by the exhaustive admit test and production is proved a subset of the mirror over the pinned catalog (`catalog.Current().Errors`) by the refusal loop, with a mirror-inside-catalog pin and fail-closed empty-domain guards. P20 (admit `terminal_backend_unavailable` for all ten ops) now fails the suite. Non-catalog strings are an unbounded domain: three probes pin the shape with the sampling bound stated, not claimed as closure.\n736|- FIX (F3): added `CheckAttachResult(false, false, auth{InputAuthorized:true})` — the case only the third conjunct catches. Dropping `resultInputAuthorized != auth.InputAuthorized` now fails the suite.\n737|- FIX (F4): attach expiry pinned from both sides — admitted one second before `expires`, refused exactly at it. `!now.Before(expires)` → `now.After(expires)` now fails the suite.\n738|- BOUNDS (carried forward, not dropped): the inventory kills every arm-deleting mutant by construction, so post-leaf-3 mutation scores are NOT comparable to leaf 2's 91/95 — stated in the inventory file's Stated bounds block and here. Attribution drift survives via the entry+code fallback — live example `CheckTransition`'s dead `\"operation vocabulary\"` arm resolving through `ParseOperation`'s test — also stated there. Declined closure: P13 (empty-ID `ProjectToLegacy` still refuses, different wire code). P11 (legacy escape name) is no longer declined: C20 (`legacyForward` gains `\"screen\"`) is killed by `TestLegacyReverseProjectionExistsOnlyForThePair`, so the closed-set property is pinned.\n739|- EVIDENCE: A1/A2/P8/P16/P20 replayed, each red with exit 1, tree restored byte-identical (shasum). Full gates re-run below.\n740|- SCOPE: `internal/terminalbackend/refusal_arm_inventory_test.go` (derivation + bounds), `conformance_test.go` (F2–F4); `LOGBOOK.md` (this entry, 89.9% correction). No production change, no table change, README sentence stands as written now that the derivation covers it.\n741|- STATUS: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (14/14), `-race` on terminalbackend exit 0, `go vet ./...` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` exit 0 (`acceptance_cases=76`, section coverage unchanged). Package coverage 90.0% statements measured on this rework tree (test-only additions vs the rev-1 tree the reviewer measured at 89.9%). Rework left uncommitted in the working tree per the brief (board checkpoints, no commit).\n742|\n743|### TASK-260830-1snnef round-2 rework: three sampled closures of one family, closed by derivation\n744|- FINDING (G2): `TestPlainErrorsLiveOnlyInTheirTwoFunctions` walked FuncDecl bodies only — the exact walk `deriveRefusalArms` was extended past in round 1, 200 lines above in the same file. Identical `errors.New` text was red in a FuncDecl and green in a package-level var (W5b), `fmt.Errorf` likewise (W9b), var func literal likewise (W16).\n745|- FIX (G2): the sibling walk gained the same GenDecl/ValueSpec loop (shared `isPlainErrorConstruction` helper, receiver-qualified method names). Twin-hunt over the story boundary (`internal/terminalbackend` AST walks): `deriveRefusalArms` already extended, `rejectConstructorAliases` inspects whole files, `productionCodeSymbols` walks package-level const GenDecls by construction, `testBodies`/`predicateCodes` are func-scoped by convention and fail closed, the platform funnel is function-scoped by design. No other twin. Bonus kill: an unused package-level plain-error var (W18 shape) is now red too — its initializer runs at package init, so the construction is real.\n746|- FIX (G1): `TestCheckStatusResultEnforcesLookupRules` now derives the complement — every state the production parser admits (`derivedParserVocabulary` over the switch-case list) outside parked/active is refused with attach evidenced; parked/active admitted. C13/C26/C27/C28/C29 each red, C30 still red.\n747|- FIX (G3): new internal `TestReplicationMembersAreExactlyTheClosedTable` pins the live `replicationMembers` map in both directions plus the size (64 members). C40c (add) and C40-init-injection red there; C40b/C40d red there and at the entry. External test comment restated to its half (want subset production) with the reverse cited.\n748|- FIX (G4): new `TestDerivedVocabulariesAreExactlyTheAdmittedSets` derives all four parser vocabularies (states, operations, effects, transports) from switch-case lists resolved through string consts, both directions plus size, and pins `conformanceOperations` to the derived operation set — the \"pinned by\" citation now holds. Refused samples restated as sampling bounds over the unbounded string domain and extended with the reviewer's exact survivor strings (`detached`, `detach`, `input_reopened`, `ssh_tunnel`), each now behaviorally refused.\n749|- BOUNDS (recorded, not closed): W11 (DigestFile allowlist is function-wide, no detail pin), W13 (bespoke error types outside both spellings), mismatchf format-verb interpolation (derivation now fatals on any constructor call without exactly one string-literal argument — zero such sites today; vet catches non-constant formats). P11 stale bound dropped (C20 killed); P13 declined closure stands.\n750|- TOOLING: round-3 runner (`.temp/TASK-260830-1snnef-r2/probe.py` family successor `.temp/TASK-260830-1snnef-r3/probe3.py`) snapshots and hash-verifies every touched file regardless of extension, with a JSON-restore self-test and a porcelain+fingerprint tree-identity check — a T01-shaped JSON mutation can no longer contaminate the tree.\n751|- EVIDENCE: 21/21 replayed red, 0 survived, 0 anchor-missing (G1x6 incl. control, G2x5 incl. control and unused-var, G3x4 incl. init injection and both reclassifications, G4x5 incl. control, F2 guard). Tree verified identical before/after (porcelain + watched hashes).\n752|- SCOPE: `internal/terminalbackend/conformance_test.go` (G1/G3-comment/G4), `internal_pin_test.go` (G3 pin), `refusal_arm_inventory_test.go` (G2 twin + single-arg assertion + bounds), `LOGBOOK.md` (this entry + P11 correction). No production change, no arm-table change, 193/193 undisturbed.\n753|- STATUS: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (14/14), `-race` on terminalbackend exit 0, `go vet ./...` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` exit 0 (`acceptance_cases=76`, `clauses_discharged=17/403`). Package coverage 90.0% statements. Rework left uncommitted in the working tree per the brief (board checkpoints, no commit).","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
