{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c7f9","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06ff2-73b2-7750-92a2-8ff950295c9d"},"sequence":599,"recorded_at":1780531400001193,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"1b11d441-f4bd-4331-a485-e0ecf0af0397","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"1b11d441-f4bd-4331-a485-e0ecf0af0397","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"1b11d441-f4bd-4331-a485-e0ecf0af0397"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"2a7c1e96-02d4-4405-87c8-7878f02883d9"},"task_id":"2a7c1e96-02d4-4405-87c8-7878f02883d9","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"2a7c1e96-02d4-4405-87c8-7878f02883d9","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-16-1\",\n  \"command\": \"cat >> LOGBOOK.md <<'EOF'\\n\\n### TASK-260830-1snnef round-3 rework: unpinned legacyForward closed by a white-box pin, plus a correction\\n- CORRECTION: the round-1 and round-2 entries above claim C20 (`legacyForward` gains `\\\"screen\\\"`) is killed by `TestLegacyReverseProjectionExistsOnlyForThePair` and drop the P11 bound on that basis. That claim is false, and the error is the reviewer's (round-2 verdict), not the producer's — the rework followed the verdict. C20 lands on `BuiltinTmux` while `ProjectToLegacy` iterates a map, so the kill was a coin flip over iteration order: 5 red and 7 green across 12 runs of the reviewer's own probe. A single red on a map-iteration mutant proves nothing. LESSON, applied to every mutant below: a mutant over map iteration (or anything else iterating a map, e.g. `ProjectToLegacy`) is run repeatedly before its verdict is believed.\\n- FIX (H1, blocking): new white-box `TestLegacyForwardIsExactlyTheImmutablePair` (`internal_pin_test.go`) holds the live `legacyForward` map to exactly `{tmux, conpty}` in both directions plus the size — the `replicationMembers` idiom from this same CR — and additionally pins injectivity (distinct canonical values), which `ProjectToLegacy`'s documented determinism rested on unenforced. The black-box forward comment is restated to its half (sampling bound, not closure) with the reverse cited, and the reviewer's escape strings join the refused samples (`TranslateLegacyBackend(\\\"screen\\\")`, `ProjectToLegacy(\\\"vendor.screen\\\")`).\\n- FIX (H2, bound, closed cheaply): new `rejectPlainErrorAliases` fails the suite on any `errors.New`/`fmt.Errorf`-kin reference outside direct-call position, in every function including the two allowlisted ones (an alias inside `validatePlatforms` would bypass the funneled detail pin). Stated bounds and the allowlist test comment record the closure. Bespoke error types outside both spellings remain the disclosed bound.\\n- EVIDENCE: L3 (`\\\"screen\\\": \\\"vendor.screen\\\"`) 12/12 red, C20 (`\\\"screen\\\": BuiltinTmux`) 12/12 red, each over `-run TestLegacy|TestHistorical`; the new pin alone red on C20 with the size message (`holds 3 names, want exactly 2`); H2 alias (`var newPlain = errors.New` + call from a FuncDecl) 3/3 red on `TestPlainErrors`. Tree verified identical before/after (file-content compare + restore assert).\\n- SCOPE: `internal/terminalbackend/internal_pin_test.go` (H1 pin), `conformance_test.go` (H1 comment + 2 samples), `refusal_arm_inventory_test.go` (H2 alias gate + bounds), `LOGBOOK.md` (this entry). No production change, no arm-table change, 193/193 undisturbed.\\n- STATUS: gates re-run below. Rework left uncommitted in the working tree per the brief (board checkpoints, no commit).\\nEOF\\necho appended\",\n  \"description\": \"Append logbook correction entry\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"appended\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 9,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 3,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}"}}}
